    "summary": "Ran the cross-cutting proof and turned daemon threads on by default. Flipping the default exposed three defects, all fixed. (1) @lancedb/lancedb 0.27.2 crashed the process when one thread searched while another wrote; it is upgraded to 0.40.0, with a cross-thread regression test that fails on 0.27.2, and compactEntityVecTable now prunes twice for 0.40's behaviour. (2) Index-run figures and registry status never left the code-indexing worker; they now go through the status board, with the store slot published before the runs. (3) The repo-completeness test raced on that publish order. Added the admin p99 latency and session-request isolation tests and a daemon-ctl smoke test. The full sweep shows 678 of 681 files passing; two of the failures predate this work (sqlite-driver temporalTrend integer overflow, review-decision /var vs /private/var), and the third (repo-completeness) has been fixed and passed 5 of 5 runs.",
